// The boss journal: Brannoc the Undefeated, champion of the drowned colosseum, in each hero's own words (docs/plans/journal-voices.md)
// Brannoc has no spoken lines in the journal; the heroes speak for him. Move keys are cast names (the journal fires on the cast bar's name).
// Banner Fall lives inside Sunwheel (Act II); Riptide lives inside Breaker (the painted path shows how often the wave returns).
// Rebound is the wheel thrown at the shield (a ring follows him, then holds, and the road is drawn to it); on Hard the caught wheel is kicked back (Riposte).
// Twin Wheels, Double Grip and Riposte are the Hard-only pages.
(window.JOURNAL_DATA = window.JOURNAL_DATA || {}).brannoc = {
  // the first time this hero meets him (after the first pull)
  meet: {
    bastion: "Champion of an arena that sank long ago, still fighting for a crowd that left it. He throws a round bronze shield, and it bounces off the walls on a road drawn on the sand before it moves. One of us stands where it rests and takes it. The rest keep off the road. Held.",
    gloomsworn: "The arena drowned long ago and the stands are full of pale faces cheering anyway. He throws a bronze shield that rebounds off the walls along a road drawn in the sand. One of us must stand in the blue ring where it ends. Cheered by the dead. I know the sensation.",
    thresher: "Such a showman, dear, and a crowd of pale ghosts in the stands who never stopped clapping. He throws his great round shield off the walls, and the whole road is drawn first in the sand. One of us waits in the blue ring where it ends. Do mind the lines, dear.",
    bloodreaver: "The big one throws a bronze wheel that bounces off every wall, and its road is drawn on the sand first, as if he wanted us to have a chance! One of us stands in the blue ring where it stops and takes the hit. The rest stay off the road. A fine arena.",
    runeguard: "The Undefeated throws a round bronze shield that rebounds from the walls; the whole road is drawn on the sand, bounce by bounce, before it moves. At its end is a blue ring: one of us must stand in it, and all the others off the road. The omen is the drawing.",
    gorgemaw: "My host is a showman who serves his courses thrown. A great bronze plate, skimmed off the walls, and the whole route drawn on the sand beforehand like a menu. One guest sits in the blue ring where it lands and takes it. The rest keep off the route. Promising.",
    oathbroker: "The Champion's instrument is a round bronze shield, thrown, rebounding off the walls. Its whole route is drawn on the sand in advance, and one of my co-signatories must stand in the blue ring at its end to receive it. All others stand clear of the route. Terms read, and for once understood.",
    ironpalm: "He speaks by throwing. A bronze wheel off the walls, and its road drawn on the sand before it moves. At the end, a ring of blue. One of us stands in it and takes the word. The rest stay off the road. Ghosts cheered him all the while. Breathe.",
    ranger: "Round shield, thrown off the walls. The whole road's drawn on the sand before it moves, bounce by bounce, ending in a blue ring. One of us stands in the ring and takes it. The rest keep off the road. Ghosts in the stands. Clean line, if you read it.",
    shadowblade: "The mark is a showman with a crowd of ghosts who never stop clapping. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls, and the road is drawn on the sand before it flies, which is very sporting of him. One of us stands where it ends. The rest are elsewhere. It never saw me.",
    pyromancer: "He throws a blazing bronze wheel off every wall and a crowd of ghosts roars for him! I was jealous. The road is drawn on the sand first, with a blue ring at the end, where one of us has to stand and take it. The rest keep off the road. Fine entrance, that.",
    thermist: "A drowned arena, a crowd of pale ghosts, a bronze wheel bouncing off the walls on a road drawn on the sand. One of us stands in the blue ring at its end. Everyone else off the road. I wanted the ring myself, and ran too warm for it.",
    driftblade: "He throws a bronze wheel off the walls and the whole road is drawn on the sand first, bounce by bounce, so I watched it drawn and ran round it, never landing, while one of us stood in the blue ring at the end and took it.",
    alembist: "Specimen: one champion, very loud, in a drowned arena, with a crowd of pale ghosts. Throws a bronze wheel off the walls, route drawn on the sand beforehand. Note: one of us stands in the blue ring where it ends. Everyone else off the route. Label: do not touch the wheel.",
    threadweaver: "A great loud lump in a drowned arena, with a crowd of ghosts clapping for him. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls, and the road is drawn in the sand first. One of my stitches stands in the blue ring at the end. The rest keep off the road.",
    marionettist: "The star of a drowned arena, with a house full of ghosts who never stop applauding. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls, and the blocking is chalked on the sand before it moves. One of the company stands in the blue ring at the end. The rest stay off the chalk.",
    cleric: "He fights for a crowd of ghosts now, poor soul, and they cheer him still. He throws a bronze shield off the walls, and the road is drawn on the sand first. One of my dear ones stands in the blue ring where it ends. The rest keep off the road.",
    grovekeeper: "A big loud fellow in a drowned arena, with ghosts for weather. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls like a stone off a pond, and the whole road is drawn on the sand first. One of my lot stands in the blue ring where it lands. The rest keep off the road.",
    chronomancer: "A champion with an audience that died long before he did, or after. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls, and the road is drawn on the sand first. One of us stands in the blue ring where it ends; the rest stay off the road. I will have been right about the ring.",
    tidecaller: "A drowned arena, and the sea still lapping at the sand. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls like a skipped stone, and the road is drawn first. One of us stands in the blue ring where it ends. The rest keep off the road. The ghosts cheered the whole while. Mind the tide.",
    lanternkeeper: "A drowned arena, and stands of pale lamps that never go out. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls, and its road is drawn on the sand first. One of us stands in the blue ring where it ends; I lit it first. The rest keep off the road. Walk where it's warm.",
    kenseier: "A loud pit-fighter, with ghosts in the stands. He throws a bronze wheel off the walls, and the road is drawn on the sand before it moves, bounce by bounce. One of us stands in the blue ring at its end. The rest stay off the road. Honest, for a show-off.",
    houndmaster: "Big lad in a sunk arena, ghosts in the stands cheering him on. Throws a bronze wheel off the walls. Whole road's drawn on the sand first. One of us stands in the blue ring where it stops; the rest keep off the road. Dogs off the sand altogether. Sit.",
  },
  // the first time this hero beats him
  win: {
    bastion: "The sea took him back, and the ring of stone is quiet. He fought a whole bout and then another, and never once stopped. Undefeated, until now. Every one of us walked out standing.",
    gloomsworn: "The sea took the big fellow back. The stands are empty now, and I suspect he knew the crowd was gone and fought anyway. I took off my helm to him.",
    thresher: "He sank back into the sea with his arms up, dear, as if the crowd were still there. Perhaps for him it was. His name is off the list at last.",
    bloodreaver: "The big one went down, then up as a titan, then down again, and I have scars from every round! The finest bout of my life. Bow, everyone. The crowd can go home now.",
    runeguard: "The Undefeated is defeated, and it is entered in the margin with every bank shot and its omen. I allow myself one flourish: the ghosts in the stands rose to him, and, at the last, to us.",
    gorgemaw: "The sea took my host, and the sand drank the rest. A gaudy, bombastic, bouncing meal, and I ate every course of it, titan and all. I am nearly full. Ask me when the crowd goes home.",
    oathbroker: "The Champion's undefeated status is lapsed, the sea standing witness. The crowd of ghosts, having paid nothing, was well entertained. The match is concluded, and the title, unclaimed, returns to the water.",
    ironpalm: "He spoke loudly all night, and in the end we answered. The sea took him back. The stands went quiet, and the ghosts bowed.",
    ranger: "Down. Sea took him. Stands empty. Every bounce read, every ring filled. Walked off the stone without a scratch worth the mention.",
    shadowblade: "The mark finally took his bow, and for once he saw nothing but the sea. A grand finish, the kind he'd have loved. The ghosts cheered us out. Soft applause.",
    pyromancer: "The sea took him, and the ghosts stood up and CHEERED us! The titan, the flood, the crowd on its feet: the best house I have ever shared a stage with. I'm hoarse, and I would do it all again tonight.",
    thermist: "The champion is down, and the sea is still, and I am exactly the temperature of the room for once. Perfect balance. Wrote it on my cuff. The ghosts applauded, which was nice.",
    driftblade: "He went down into the sea and I ran the whole ring of stone just because I could, through the spray and round the columns and back, and the ghosts cheered every lap, and my boots hardly touched.",
    alembist: "Logged at last: the champion, at rest in the sea. Samples of sand sealed; flasks mostly intact; one wheel-shaped dent in my satchel. Labels: do not open until the ghosts have gone home. Never so pleased.",
    threadweaver: "The sea took the big lump back and the ghosts clapped us out. Every thread of mine is still tied to someone, and that is the only score I keep. Come and sit by me, all of you. Kettle's on.",
    marionettist: "Curtain, at last, on the champion of the drowned house. He took his bow from the sea, and the ghosts in the stands rose for the whole company. (Ovation, from the dead, which counts. The Doll curtseyed twice.)",
    cleric: "The crowd is quiet at last, and the poor soul is at rest. We all walked off the stone on our own feet. I said a small prayer for the champion and a larger one of thanks.",
    grovekeeper: "The champion has gone back to the sea like an old tide, dear. The ghosts have gone quiet in the stands. My whole lot walked off the stone. Sit. Tea. Leave a cup for the ghosts.",
    chronomancer: "The champion fell, and the ghosts rose for him, and for us. Nobody had to be undone. The last bell never tolled for us, and I have seldom been so glad to keep only one account of an evening.",
    tidecaller: "The sea took him back the way it takes all things, without hurry. The stands emptied, the water went slack. I sang over him, low, a little.",
    lanternkeeper: "Four of us walked off the stone. I lit one small lamp on the sand where he fell and left it burning for the crowd. They had been cheering a long time.",
    kenseier: "He is down, and the sea is calm. Every throw had its count, and the last was his own. The ghosts stood in the stands, and I bowed to him. A fine bout, from a loud man.",
    houndmaster: "Big lad's gone down to the sea and the stands are quiet. Dogs came out wet and cheerful, Rust shaking sand over everything. Supper was loud.",
  },
  moves: {
    'Sunwheel': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He threw, and the road drew itself across the sand, bounce by bounce. I took the blue ring at its end and braced for the weight; the others stayed off the road, and off the wall where the banners come down.",
      gloomsworn: "The wheel's road was drawn bounce by bounce before it flew. Someone has to stand where it ends, or it bursts on all of us. I stood there. It was a heavy blow, and I carried it as I carry the rest. Everyone else kept off the road and the walls.",
      thresher: "He sends his great wheel off the walls, dear, and the whole road is painted first, so do read it. One of us waits in the blue ring at the end, and the rest stay off the road, and off the walls where the banners drop.",
      bloodreaver: "The wheel came off the walls and I stood in the blue ring to take it. It hurt wonderfully! If nobody catches it, it bursts on everyone. The rest stayed off the road and clear of the banners the bounces shook loose.",
      runeguard: "The omen: his chin points at a wall, and the road draws itself bounce by bounce. The answer: one of us in the blue ring where it rests, the others off every stripe of the road, and clear of the banners the bounces knock down.",
      gorgemaw: "A plate skimmed off the walls, route drawn first like a menu. I sat in the blue ring where it landed and ate it whole, for it bursts over every plate if no one does. The rest kept off the route and the falling banners. Brassy, and a little flat.",
      oathbroker: "The route is entered on the sand before the wheel moves. One party stands in the blue ring at its end and takes delivery in full; if none does, it is payable by all. Every other party stays off the route and from under the banners.",
      ironpalm: "He threw, and the road drew itself. At its end, a ring of blue. I stood in it and took the word whole. The others stayed off the road, and away from the walls where banners fall.",
      ranger: "Wheel off three walls, road painted first. Blue ring at the end. One of us stood in it and took it. Nobody else on the road, none by the wall where a banner drops. If the ring's empty it bursts on all of us.",
      shadowblade: "The mark tilted his chin at a wall, and the road drew itself, which is very considerate. One of us stood in the blue ring at the end, someone with more shoulder than I have. The rest of us were off the road and clear of the banners.",
      pyromancer: "He hurled the wheel and the whole road glowed the colour of trouble before it even moved! One of us stood in the blue ring where it ended and took it; the rest kept off the road and clear of the banners. I resented moving mid-cast.",
      thermist: "Chin to a wall, the road draws itself, a blue ring waits at the end. One of us stands in it. Nobody on the road, nobody under a falling banner. I ran hot watching it fly, and the wheel was already past.",
      driftblade: "The road drew itself bounce by bounce and I went round it and through the gap and out the far side, light on my feet, while one of us stood in the blue ring at the end and took the wheel, and the banners fell on empty sand.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a bronze wheel, three bounces, route drawn first. Remedy: one of us in the blue ring where it rests, to catch it, or it bursts on everyone. All others off the route and from under the banners. Note: mend the catcher before, not after.",
      threadweaver: "The wheel's road ran across the sand like a seam, drawn before it moved. One of my stitches stood at the blue ring at the end and caught it; the rest kept off the seam and from under the banners. A neat catch.",
      marionettist: "Blocking, chalked on the sand before the scene: bounce after bounce, and a mark in blue where it ends. One of the company takes the mark and catches the wheel. The rest keep off the chalk and out from under the falling banners. (The Doll kept to the wings.)",
      cleric: "He threw the wheel and its road was drawn first, bounce by bounce. One of my dear ones stood in the blue ring at the end, and I laid the light on them before the catch, not after. The rest kept off the road and the banners.",
      grovekeeper: "The wheel skipped off the walls like a flat stone, the road drawn before it flew. I'd planted on the one standing in the blue ring, for the catch is heavy. My lot stayed off the road and from under the banners.",
      chronomancer: "The road draws itself first, then the wheel follows it exactly, a beat behind the drawing. One of us stood in the blue ring and caught it; I will have mended them early, and did. The rest stayed off the road and away from the banners.",
      tidecaller: "A wheel skipped off the walls like a flat stone across a bay, and the road was drawn before it flew. One of us stood in the blue ring where it came to rest; I raised the water around them first. The rest stayed off the road.",
      lanternkeeper: "The road was drawn before it moved, so I hung a light on whoever stood in the blue ring at the end, and it was burning before the wheel arrived. Everyone else kept off the road and the banners. One on the catcher, the rest of us out of the way.",
      kenseier: "The wheel's road is drawn before it flies, and its last bounce has a beat I could count. I stood in the blue ring and met the wheel with the blade as it landed. The others stayed off the road and from under the banners.",
      houndmaster: "Wheel off the walls, road drawn first. One of us stood in the blue ring where it stopped and took it; the rest, dogs too, kept off the road and from under the banners. Plain enough, once the road's drawn.",
    } },
    'Victory Leap': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He leapt and a ring fell on one of us and followed him round, then held still. The line cleared out of it in time. When he landed and struck his pose, we hit him hard: he stood open, and let us.",
      gloomsworn: "A ring settled on one of us and followed him until it chose its ground. We cleared out of it. He landed and posed for his ghosts, open to the last. A man posing in front of the dead is easy to hit. We hit him.",
      thresher: "Up he goes, dear, and a great ring settles on one of us and follows them about until it stops. Out of it, everybody! Then he lands and bows to the crowd, and that is the moment to strike him.",
      bloodreaver: "He jumped, and a ring chased one of us until it held still! I wanted it. But the ring is for running, not taking, so we all got out. He landed and posed, wide open, and we hit him with everything.",
      runeguard: "Before the Champion vanishes upward, the sign is plain; a ring then follows one of us. Lead it away from the others and leave it when it holds. He lands and poses, which is his weakness; strike hard in that opening.",
      gorgemaw: "My host leapt, and a ring followed one guest about until it set. We left the table and let it fall on bare floor. Then he landed and posed for the stands, wide open, and I took a very large bite.",
      oathbroker: "A ring is entered against one of us and follows the named party until it sets. The remaining parties vacate it. Upon landing he poses, which waives his guard for the term of the pose; we collected on it in full.",
      ironpalm: "He leapt, and a ring followed one of us, then went still. We left it. He landed and posed, loudly, with his guard down. We answered then, all at once.",
      ranger: "He jumps. Ring follows one of us, then holds. Led it off from the rest, left it. He lands and poses for the stands. No guard. That's the shot. Everyone loosed at once.",
      shadowblade: "He vanished upward and a ring chose one of us. They led it away from the rest and slipped out when it held. Then he landed and struck a pose with his back wide open, rude of him. I took full advantage.",
      pyromancer: "He leapt out of sight and a ring the size of a stage fell on one of us and followed them! They led it off and we all got out before it held. Then he posed, wide open, for his ghosts, and I gave him a better show.",
      thermist: "A ring on one of us, following, then holding. Lead it off, leave it. Then he landed and posed, guard down, and I ran hot, burning every last thing I had into the opening.",
      driftblade: "A ring dropped on one of us and followed them round the sand until it stopped, and everybody ran out of it, through and away, and then he landed and struck a pose and we all went in at once, because posing is not guarding.",
      alembist: "Observed: a large ring drops on one of us and follows, then fixes in place. Lead it off, and have everyone out before it holds. He poses on landing with his guard down; pour in everything you have mixed. Label: do not dawdle.",
      threadweaver: "A ring fell on one of my stitches and followed along the thread until it held still. We pulled clear of it, the chosen one leading it away from the rest. Then he landed and struck a pose, and we let him have it.",
      marionettist: "A ring lowered onto one of the company and followed them across the stage until it held. The company exited it, stage left. Our star landed and struck a pose for the house, wide open, and we struck back. (Applause for the Doll.)",
      cleric: "He leapt away, and a ring settled on one of our friends and followed them until it held still. I called everyone out of it, and the chosen one led it from the rest. He landed and posed with his guard down.",
      grovekeeper: "He leapt like a stone thrown at the sky, and a ring came down on one of my lot and followed them till it set. We cleared out of it. Then he landed and posed for his crowd, wide open. That is the hour to strike.",
      chronomancer: "The ring follows its mark, then holds, just ahead of his landing. We were out of it by then. He lands, and poses, and the pose is a long beat with his guard down. Everyone hit him in it.",
      tidecaller: "He went up like a wave rearing, and a ring followed one of us until it held. We drew out of it. He came down and posed, which is the slack water of him, wide open, and we struck hard.",
      lanternkeeper: "A ring followed one of us across the sand and then held. I carried their light well away from the rest, and we stepped out of it as it settled. He landed and posed with his guard down, and we struck him hard. One light moved, none lost.",
      kenseier: "A ring follows one of us, and stops a breath before he lands. We left it. He landed and posed, which is a rest between strokes with no guard in it, and we cut into that rest together. A show-off's courtesy.",
      houndmaster: "Big lad jumped. Ring followed one of us, then stood still. Led it off from the lot of us, dogs too. He landed and posed for the stands, guard down. That's when we went in. Sit. Then go.",
    } },
    'Hammer Heel': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Two stamps, one after the other, each at my feet, the second bigger. I waited for the shoulder to drop and held for both. The others kept out of the ring around me, and the healer had me ready for the second.",
      gloomsworn: "He stamped at me twice, the second harder. The ring around me was wide and I stood in it alone. A wound is only a wound; mine are written down already. The rest stayed out, and the healer saved her best for the second.",
      thresher: "Two great stamps for our shield, dear, one right after the other, and the second is bigger. The rest of us stay out of the ring that follows him, and the healer saves her best for the second.",
      bloodreaver: "Two stamps, the second bigger, and the ring followed me wherever I went! I took both and the others stayed far out of it. Delicious. The second is the one to be ready for.",
      runeguard: "His heel lifts, a ring appears about the shield, and two stamps follow, the second the heavier. Margin note: the rest of us stand wide of the ring, and the healer's best ward is laid for the second, not the first.",
      gorgemaw: "Two courses, served to the man in front: a stamp, and a bigger one after. The ring around me followed me, so the rest of the guests stayed back. I swallowed both. Heavy, and a little dry.",
      oathbroker: "Two instalments, payable by whoever stands in front, the second larger. The ring follows the debtor; the other parties stay out of it. The healer reserves the larger cover for the second. I accepted both.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke twice with his heel, the second louder. The ring stayed on me, and the others stayed out of it. I took the first word and the second.",
      ranger: "Two stamps on the shield. Ring follows him. Second's bigger. Kept well out of it. Healer saved the best for the second. Easy to read from out here.",
      shadowblade: "The mark stamped at our shield twice, the second harder, which was rude. The ring followed him, so I stayed far from it, behind. The healer kept her best for the second.",
      pyromancer: "He stamped at the knight twice, the second harder, and a ring glowing like a forge followed him around! I kept well out of it and burned from the edge of the sand. The healer saved her best for the second.",
      thermist: "Two stamps on the shield, the second bigger, a ring following him. Stay out of it. The healer keeps her best for the second. I flinched at the first anyway, and ran cold for a moment.",
      driftblade: "Two stamps, the second bigger, both at the shield, and the ring followed him round the sand, so I stayed out of it, round and through and away, and the healer saved her best for the second.",
      alembist: "Two stamps on the shield, the second heavier, and a ring following him. Prescription: the rest of us outside the ring, and the big brew held back for the second stamp. Spent on the first, it is wasted.",
      threadweaver: "Two stamps on our shield, the second harder, and a ring followed him as if tied to him. We kept off the ring. I mended him after the first and ran the thread tight before the second.",
      marionettist: "Two stamps aimed at our shield, the second bigger, with a ring following him across the stage. The company stayed out of the circle. (The healer held her best line for the second. Good timing.)",
      cleric: "He stamped at our knight twice, the second harder. The ring followed him, so the rest of us kept out. I laid a light on him before the second, not after.",
      grovekeeper: "Two stamps at the shield, like thunder twice over, the second the worse. The ring followed him round and my lot kept out of it. I'd planted on him before the first, and again before the second.",
      chronomancer: "Two stamps, and the second is the one that matters. The ring followed our shield about, and the rest of us stayed well out of it. I mended on the first beat and braced on the second.",
      tidecaller: "A stamp, then a larger one, on the shield alone, like a swell and its bigger sister. The ring followed him, and the rest of us stayed clear. I brought the water up high before the second.",
      lanternkeeper: "Two stamps at our shield, the second bigger, with a ring following him about. I hung a light on him for each and kept the rest of us out of the ring. One for the first, one for the heavier.",
      kenseier: "Two stamps, and the second heavier. The ring follows me. I met the first as it landed, and drew the ash about me for the second. The others stayed out of the ring. Honest blows, both.",
      houndmaster: "Two stamps at the shield-man, second bigger, ring following him. Dogs stayed well out of it. Healer saved her best for the second. Like standing near a bull's hoof.",
    } },
    'Rebound': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A blue ring followed me about the sand and let go where I stood, and the road to it was drawn off the wall before the wheel flew. I picked my ground so the road ran clear of the line, planted, and caught it.",
      gloomsworn: "A blue ring clung to me and let go where I stood, and the wheel's road was drawn off the wall to it. I chose a patch of sand that kept the road away from the others and took it whole. Heavy, but nothing I had not met before.",
      thresher: "A blue ring follows our shield about, dear, and lets go where he stands, and the wheel's road is drawn to it off the wall. So watch where he plants his feet, and keep off the stripe. An empty ring bursts on us all.",
      bloodreaver: "The wheel came for ME! A blue ring stuck to me, then let go where I stood, and its road was drawn off the wall. I picked my spot so it missed my friends, stood in the ring and took it.",
      runeguard: "A blue ring followed me, then held where I stood. Choose the ground before it lets go, so that the wheel's road, drawn off the wall, runs clear of the rest; then catch it in the ring.",
      gorgemaw: "A blue plate followed me about the table and set down where I stood, with its route drawn off the wall. I chose my chair so the route missed the other guests, and swallowed the wheel in the ring. Light portion. An empty chair, and the whole room pays.",
      oathbroker: "The terms: a blue ring follows the one in front and holds where he stood, and the wheel's route is drawn to it off the wall. I chose my ground before the ring let go, so the route missed my co-signatories, and accepted delivery.",
      ironpalm: "A ring of blue followed me, then held where I stood. The wheel's road was drawn to it off the wall. I chose where to stand before it let go, so the road passed the others by, and I caught it. Empty, it bursts on everyone.",
      ranger: "Ring follows the shield, then holds where he stood. The wheel's road is drawn to it off the wall. He picks the spot, so I watch where he plants and keep off the stripe. He catches it. Empty ring bursts on us all.",
      shadowblade: "A blue ring followed our shield about the sand and held where he stood, and the wheel's road was drawn to it off the wall. He chose his ground so the road missed us, and I stayed off the stripe.",
      pyromancer: "A blue ring chased our shield about, then let go where he stood, and the wheel came off the wall to it along a road drawn in gold! He picked his spot so it missed us and caught it, and I kept off the stripe.",
      thermist: "A blue ring follows the shield, then holds where he stood, and the wheel's road is drawn to it off the wall. He chose his ground so the stripe missed us. I stayed off it, a steady kind of cold, and watched him catch.",
      driftblade: "A blue ring followed the shield, then held where he stood, and the wheel's road was drawn to it off the wall. He picked his ground so it missed us, and I ran round the stripe, light as ever, while he caught it.",
      alembist: "Cause: a wheel thrown at our shield, its road drawn off the wall to a blue ring that follows him, then holds. Cure: he picks his ground so the road misses us, and stands in the ring. An empty ring bursts on everyone, and that is one explosion I did not plan.",
      threadweaver: "A blue ring followed our shield about, then held where he stood, and the wheel's road was drawn to it off the wall. He chose his spot so the seam missed the rest of us, and I tied him tight before the catch.",
      marionettist: "A blue mark followed our lead about the stage, then held where he stood, and the wheel's blocking was chalked to it off the wall. He chose his mark so it cleared the company and took the catch. The rest kept off the chalk.",
      cleric: "A blue ring followed our knight about the sand, then held where he stood, and the wheel's road was drawn to it off the wall. He chose his ground so it missed the rest of us. I laid the light on him before the catch, not after.",
      grovekeeper: "A blue ring followed my big fellow about, then held where he stood, and the wheel came off the wall along a road drawn first. He chose his ground so it missed my lot, and caught it. I planted on him before. We kept off the stripe.",
      chronomancer: "The ring found our shield, then held its place, and I had seen the road before it was drawn: off the wall, to him. He chose where to stand, and I mended him a beat ahead. We stayed off the stripe.",
      tidecaller: "A blue ring trailed our shield and settled where he stood, a mark on the sand, with the wheel coming off the wall to it. He picked his ground to keep the stripe from the rest of us, and I swelled the water around him for the catch.",
      lanternkeeper: "I hung a lamp on our shield when the blue ring took him, and the ring stayed where he stopped. The wheel's road was drawn from the champion's hand and off the wall to it. He had chosen well. We waited in the dark, off the stripe.",
      kenseier: "A blue ring followed me, then held where I stood, and the wheel's road was drawn to it off the wall. I chose my ground before it let go, so the road passed the others by, and I met the catch with the blade. Honest, for a thrown wheel.",
      houndmaster: "Big lad flung a wheel at the shield-man. Blue ring stuck to him, then held where he stood, and the road was drawn to it off the wall. He picked his ground so it missed us and the dogs, and caught it. Dogs off the stripe.",
    } },
    'Roar of the Stands': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The stands roared and it reached every one of us at once. A shield has no edge to put against a noise. I planted my feet, the line closed up near the healer, and we took it together, already mended.",
      gloomsworn: "The ghosts in the stands roared, and the sound reached every one of us. A shield turns nothing like that. We stood close to the healer, mended beforehand, and let it pass through us as it passes through the dead.",
      thresher: "All those pale ghosts in the stands shout at once, dear, and it reaches every corner. Come to it mended and close together. It is quite the ovation. Do mind your hat.",
      bloodreaver: "The whole crowd roared and it hit every one of us! Nothing to dodge, so I stood by the healer and let it blow. Not much of a scar, but a loud one.",
      runeguard: "The stands draw breath, and the roar that follows reaches every one of us; no ward turns it. One prepares by being mended and gathered before it breaks.",
      gorgemaw: "The crowd's applause came down on every guest at once, a cold sauce over every plate. No guest can swallow it for another. We sat close to the healer, mended beforehand, and drank it down. Thin, but loud.",
      oathbroker: "The stands' levy is a general roar, owed by every party together with no exemption. The remedy is to arrive whole and close to the healer, and so we paid it and remained solvent.",
      ironpalm: "The stands spoke, all at once, to all of us. Nothing to turn aside. We were close and mended, and the word went over us.",
      ranger: "Crowd roars. Whole room takes it. No cover, no lane. Mended first, grouped near the healer. It blows through.",
      shadowblade: "The ghosts roared and every one of us felt it. No back to slip behind; a crowd has none. I stood close to the healer, mended beforehand, and let it by. Rude of them to make such a noise.",
      pyromancer: "The crowd roared and it hit all of us, and not one patch of floor to hide on! I stood close to the healer, mended beforehand, and went on casting through it. A louder audience than mine; I asked about the booking.",
      thermist: "The crowd roars, everyone takes it, no dodge. Mended first, close to the healer. My ears rang hot for a while after, but I stayed on my feet with my hands still working.",
      driftblade: "The whole crowd roared and it caught everyone and there was no running round it, so I ran in close to the healer, whole, and took it standing nearly still, which I hate.",
      alembist: "A roar across the whole room, and no cover to stand behind, so the only thing left to improve is the dose. Everyone gathered close; the big brew goes in before it lands, not after.",
      threadweaver: "The roar went down every thread together. I pulled my stitches in close and had them mended before it hit, not after. Nobody was shaken loose.",
      marionettist: "The house roared, the whole house at once, and the sound reached every seat. The company gathered close to the healer, mended beforehand, and took it as one. (A very loud ovation. Not for us.)",
      cleric: "The crowd roared and it came over every one of us at once. I gathered everyone close and laid the light on them before it came, not after, and all of them stood up straight.",
      grovekeeper: "The roar of the stands came down like a hard frost over the whole garden. Everyone had roots in them already, and my lot stood close, so the mending was waiting before the frost.",
      chronomancer: "The roar comes on the heels of his lifted arms, every time. I had everyone mended and close in the moment before. It passed without anyone being undone.",
      tidecaller: "A swell of sound from the stands, reaching every one of us, no shelter anywhere. I brought the water up before it came and the others drew in close, so it broke on a full shore.",
      lanternkeeper: "The stands roared over every one of us. I hung a light on each of us before it came, and we stood close by the glow. Four lights, four of us.",
      kenseier: "A roar across the whole arena, and no blade turns a roar. We stood in beside the healer, mended beforehand, and outlasted it.",
      houndmaster: "Whole crowd roared and it reached the lot of us, dogs too. No dodging a noise. Pair of them tucked in by the healer, mended before it hit, and we sat it out.",
    } },
    'Sand Furrow': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He dragged his heel through the sand and a long strip across the room was marked. We stood off it when it struck, and it stayed churned and biting for a good while after. The line kept to its own side.",
      gloomsworn: "A long furrow, dragged across the whole arena, and it stays. Whoever stands in it bleeds long after the blow has fallen. I stepped off it and stayed off. Even I know better than to lie in a grave twice.",
      thresher: "He drags his heel across the sand, dear, and a long strip is cut through the whole room, and it stays churned a good while. So step off at once, and keep off, and cross it only when you must.",
      bloodreaver: "He ploughed the sand clear across the room, and it hurt where it landed and went on hurting! I like a lasting wound, but not that one. We stepped off it, and stayed off, and kept to our sides.",
      runeguard: "His heel drags, and a long strip is marked across the whole room. Leave it before it strikes and do not return, for the churned sand keeps its bite a long while; it cuts the room in two, so plan the next catch accordingly.",
      gorgemaw: "My host drew his heel across the floor like a knife across a cloth, and the cut stayed. We stepped off before it fell, and stayed off; it bites for a long while. A room cut in two is a poor table. Sour.",
      oathbroker: "A furrow is entered across the whole floor. It falls once, hard, and thereafter bears interest for a long term. Clause one: vacate it at once and stay off, and plan the crossing, for the floor is now two parcels.",
      ironpalm: "He dragged his heel and the sand spoke a long line across the room. I stepped off it before it fell, and stayed off. It spoke for a long while after.",
      ranger: "Heel dragged across the sand. Long strip, whole room. Stepped off before it fell, stayed off. It bites a long while. Cuts the room in half; plan the crossing. Fine, so long as you stay on your side.",
      shadowblade: "The mark dragged his heel through the sand and cut the room in two. I stepped off the strip before it fell and stayed off, because it bites for a long while. A crude way to keep people apart.",
      pyromancer: "He dragged his heel through the sand and a strip across the whole room went an angry orange! I stepped off before it struck and stayed off, because it burns long after. Frankly, it was the sand's fault.",
      thermist: "A long strip across the room, falls hard, then keeps biting. Step off before, stay off. I stood in it for one breath and felt every grain scald. It cuts the room in two, so plan the crossing.",
      driftblade: "He dragged his heel across the sand and cut the room in two, so I slipped across before it fell and out the far side, and kept to one side after, because it bites a long while, and I hate being fenced in.",
      alembist: "Result of the dragged heel: a furrow across the whole room, striking once and then lingering. Step off before it falls, stay off while it lasts, and plan the next catch, since the floor is now in two halves. Do not stand in the sediment.",
      threadweaver: "He dragged a heel and the sand split like a seam across the whole room. We stepped off before it struck and kept off, for the churned sand bites a long while. A room cut in two is a sloppy hem.",
      marionettist: "A long line dragged across the stage, and then it stays: a trench down the middle of the set. The company cleared it before it struck and kept to their own side after. (Two halves, one act. Tricky.)",
      cleric: "He dragged his heel and a long strip of the room was marked, and it stayed hurtful after. I called everyone off it before it fell and kept them off. A room cut in two, and all of mine on one side.",
      grovekeeper: "He ploughed the sand clear across the room like a furrow ploughed the wrong way, and it kept its bite a good while. We stepped off before it fell and stayed off. Nothing grows in that row. Plant first, elsewhere.",
      chronomancer: "The heel drags, and the strip strikes on a beat, and then it keeps biting for a long while after. We stepped off before the beat and stayed off. It cuts the room in two. The crossings were planned before he stood up.",
      tidecaller: "He drew his heel through the sand like a rip current, a long strip across the room that bites after. We stepped out before it fell and kept out. It parts the room as a channel parts a beach.",
      lanternkeeper: "A long strip was marked across the whole room, and it stays hurtful a good while. I picked our light up and set it down on one side, off the strip, and we kept to it. A room cut in two wants a light on each side.",
      kenseier: "His heel drags a strip across the room. The first stroke falls hard, and the sand goes on biting for a long while. We stepped off before it fell and stayed off. It divides the room; plan where the next throw lands.",
      houndmaster: "Big lad dragged his boot and cut the room in two. Stepped off before it fell, called the dogs off it, kept clear. Sand bites a good while after. Sit. Like walking a dog round a ploughed field.",
    } },
    'The Tide Rises': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The sand turned to sea and he rose out of it, too far above to reach. The water broke over every one of us at once, and no shield turns it. We came to it mended and close, and it set us down on a ring of stone.",
      gloomsworn: "The colosseum drowned all over again. He rose from the water, beyond reach, and the flood came over every one of us. I have been under worse. We came to it close to the healer and landed on a ring of stone.",
      thresher: "The stands break up and the sea comes in, dear, and he rises out of it, quite out of reach, and the flood reaches all of us at once. Come to it mended and close. It sets us down on a ring of stone.",
      bloodreaver: "The floor flooded and the big one rose out of the sea, and I could not reach him to hit him! The water hit all of us at once. Nothing to dodge, so I stayed by the healer, and it set us down on a ring of stone.",
      runeguard: "The colosseum comes apart and he rises from the water, beyond all reach. Be mended and gathered, for the flood strikes everyone, and then keep to the ring of stone it leaves us on. The ring of stone was the one thing the omen kept from me.",
      gorgemaw: "The dining room was flooded, and my host rose out of the soup, out of reach, entirely different. The wave came over every guest at once. We came to it mended and close, and it sat us on a ring of stone. A change of menu.",
      oathbroker: "The venue is dissolved, the premises flooded, and the counterparty rises from the water, out of reach. The flood is owed by every party jointly: arrive whole and near the healer. We were then relocated to a ring of stone.",
      ironpalm: "The sand turned to water. He rose, out of reach, and the flood spoke to all of us. We were close, and mended, and it let us go. It set us down on a ring of stone. We stood on it.",
      ranger: "Floor floods. He goes up out of reach. Wave hits everyone, nowhere to stand. Mended first, grouped by the healer. Set down on a ring of stone, smaller room. No wall now, just water. Keep off the rim.",
      shadowblade: "The mark rose out of the flood, beyond even my reach, and the water found everyone. Nowhere to hide; I stood close to the healer, mended beforehand. It put us on a ring of stone in the open sea. Rude, but dramatic.",
      pyromancer: "The whole colosseum flooded and he rose out of the sea like a theatrical entrance, and I had NOTHING to burn him with! The flood hit all of us. I stood close to the healer, mended beforehand. The sea is the one audience I cannot warm.",
      thermist: "The floor floods, he rises out of reach, and the water hits everyone. I came mended and stood by the healer. Then a ring of stone in an open sea; keep off the rim. I steamed through the wave and came out too warm.",
      driftblade: "The sand turned to sea and he rose out of it, too high to reach, and the flood caught all of us, no running round it, so I ran in close to the healer and rode it out, and landed on a ring of stone in the open sea.",
      alembist: "Day's entry: the room flooded, the patient rose out of reach, and the water struck everyone. Mended and gathered beforehand, we were moved to a smaller floor, a ring of stone. Stay off the rim, it is wet.",
      threadweaver: "The stands broke up, the sea came in, and he rose out of it, out of reach. The flood went along every thread at once. I pulled my stitches in close and mended them before. We were set down on a ring of stone.",
      marionettist: "The set flooded, the house came apart, and our star rose out of the water, quite out of reach. The flood took the whole company at once; we gathered close to the healer, mended beforehand. New scene: a ring of stone in the open sea.",
      cleric: "The arena fell apart and the sea came in. He rose out of it, beyond reach, and the flood went over every one of us. I gathered them close and laid the light on them before, not after. It set us down on a ring of stone.",
      grovekeeper: "The floor flooded like a spring thaw and he rose out of it, past reach. The flood came over my whole lot at once. I'd planted on everyone before, and we stood close. It set us down on a ring of stone.",
      chronomancer: "The flood comes hard on his rising, every time. Everyone was mended and close by then. Then the ring of stone, in an open sea. He is out of reach until the water is done; there is nothing to hit.",
      tidecaller: "The tide came in all at once and the colosseum broke on it. He rose out of the sea, out of reach, and the flood reached every one of us. The water stood high in us before it came. It set us down on a ring of stone.",
      lanternkeeper: "The stands went under, and the lamps with them. He rose out of the sea, out of reach, and the flood reached every one of us. I hung a light on each before. We were set down on a ring of stone.",
      kenseier: "The sand became sea, and he rose out of it, beyond the blade. The flood reaches everyone and no blade turns water. We stood close to the healer, mended beforehand, and outlasted it. A ring of stone remained.",
      houndmaster: "Floor flooded, and the big lad went up out of reach. Wave hit the lot of us, dogs too. Whistled the pair in tight by the healer, mended before. Set us down on a ring of stone.",
    } },
    'Fist Slam': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The great fist followed me about the stone. I led it away from the line, out to the empty edge, and waited for it to stop. Everyone else was well clear of me when it fell.",
      gloomsworn: "The fist came for me alone, following me over the stone. I walked it to the empty edge, away from the others, and took it whole when it fell. Heavy, and over quickly. The rest kept clear.",
      thresher: "A great fist follows our shield about the ring, dear, so he walks it off to the empty edge, well away from the rest of us. It falls where he stands, and the healer has him ready before. Do keep clear.",
      bloodreaver: "The titan's fist chased me over the stone and I loved it! I walked it to the edge, away from my friends, and let it land. Bleed first, then drink. Nobody else was near enough to feel it.",
      runeguard: "The great fist follows the shield. Lead it to a bare edge, well away from the rest; it falls where he stands, and the healer's ward is laid beforehand. Nobody else stands near him at that moment.",
      gorgemaw: "The giant's fist, served to me alone. It follows its plate about the floor, so I carried it out to the edge, away from the rest of the guests, and swallowed it whole. Large portion, little flavour.",
      oathbroker: "The fist is owed by whoever stands in front, and follows the debtor until it falls. I led it to the empty edge, clear of my co-signatories, and accepted delivery in full. The healer's cover was laid before.",
      ironpalm: "The great fist followed me over the stone. I led it to the edge, away from the others, and when it stopped, it fell. I took it. They stood far away.",
      ranger: "Fist follows the shield. Led it to the empty edge, away from the rest. Falls where he stands. Others well clear. Healer ready before it fell.",
      shadowblade: "The titan's fist followed our shield about the stone, as it should. He walked it to the empty edge, away from the rest of us, and it fell on him alone. I kept well back.",
      pyromancer: "A fist the size of a barn followed the knight about the ring, and the whole circle glowed the colour of trouble! He led it to the empty edge and I stayed well back, casting. The healer had him ready.",
      thermist: "The fist follows the shield. Lead it to the empty edge, away from the rest, and everyone clear when it falls. I stood too close once and felt the heat of it. Too far in.",
      driftblade: "The fist followed the shield about the ring, and the shield led it out to the edge, away from us, and I stayed round the far side of the stone, through the gaps, never near it, until it fell and he took it alone.",
      alembist: "Procedure: a giant fist follows the shield, then falls. Lead it to the empty edge, away from everyone; my dose goes in before the fall. Keep clear of the shield at the moment of the slam, as with any lit fuse.",
      threadweaver: "The great fist followed our shield about the ring, like a bobbin on a thread. He led it to the empty edge, away from my stitches, and it fell on him alone. I tied him tight before. We kept clear.",
      marionettist: "The giant's fist followed our shield about the stage, and he led it to the empty edge, well away from the company, and let it fall on him alone. (The healer held the light.) We kept clear of him at the moment.",
      cleric: "The titan's fist followed our knight about the stone. He led it to the empty edge, away from the rest of us, and I laid the light on him before it fell, not after. We stayed clear.",
      grovekeeper: "The fist followed the shield about the ring like a storm following a ridge. He led it to the empty edge, away from my lot, and I'd planted on him before. We stayed far from him when it fell.",
      chronomancer: "The fist follows the shield, then holds a beat, then falls. He led it to the empty edge, away from the rest of us. I mended him just before the fall. We kept clear of him at the moment.",
      tidecaller: "The great fist rose over the shield like a swell over a rock and followed him about the ring. He led it to the empty edge, away from the rest of us, and I swelled the water round him first.",
      lanternkeeper: "The fist followed our shield, so I hung a light on him and let him lead it out to the empty edge, away from the rest of us. It fell where he stood. We kept clear. One light on the shield, three of us far off.",
      kenseier: "The fist follows me and stops a breath before it falls. I led it to the empty edge and met it with the blade as it landed, the ash drawn about me. The others were far from me when it fell. Honest, for a giant.",
      houndmaster: "Giant's fist chased the shield-man round the stone. He led it to the empty edge, away from us and the dogs, and it fell on him alone. Healer had him ready. Dogs well back, the lot of them.",
    } },
    'Breaker': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The slam threw a wave out to the rim, and it came back off the wall. The whole path was painted. I took the fist first, and the others stood behind a fallen column, out of the water's road.",
      gloomsworn: "The slam sent a wave to the rim, and the rim sent it back. The road was painted, wide as a grave. A fallen column stops it for whoever stands behind. The rest of us stood behind the columns while I took the fist.",
      thresher: "He slams, dear, and a wave runs out to the rim and comes back off it, the whole path painted first. A fallen column shelters whoever stands behind it, so do read the lines and choose your column.",
      bloodreaver: "The fist fell, and a wave ran out from it to the rim and back! I took the fist; the others hid behind fallen columns from the water. The path is painted, wide as a road.",
      runeguard: "After the fist, a wave runs from the slam to the rim and returns from it, the whole path painted. A fallen column shelters whoever stands behind it; the rest of us took cover there and watched the returning line.",
      gorgemaw: "A second course after the slam: a wave sent out to the rim and sent back, the path painted like a sauce on the plate. The columns are screens, and we ate behind them. Salty, as sea is.",
      oathbroker: "The slam carries a codicil: a wave to the rim, and the same wave returned, the whole path entered in advance. A fallen column exempts whoever stands behind it, as the first clause provides. We took the columns.",
      ironpalm: "The fist spoke, and the sea echoed it out to the rim and back. The path was painted. A fallen column breaks the echo for anyone behind it. We stood behind them.",
      ranger: "Slam, then a wave out to the rim and back. Path painted, wide. Fallen column stops it for whoever's behind. Others behind columns, off the band.",
      shadowblade: "After the slam the water ran out to the rim and back, and the whole road was painted, which is the least it could do. A fallen column shelters whoever stands behind it, and I stood behind the best one.",
      pyromancer: "The fist fell and a wave of glowing foam shot to the rim and BACK! The path was painted, bless it. I ducked behind a fallen column and cast from there. A sheltered Pyromancer is a happy one.",
      thermist: "Slam, then a wave out to the rim and back, the whole path painted. Stand behind a fallen column, off the band. I ran for the nearest one, cold with nerves, and made it.",
      driftblade: "The slam threw a wave to the rim and it came back, and the whole path was painted, so I slipped through it before the water came, round a fallen column and out of the band, and it ran past me, and I was never wet.",
      alembist: "A slam, then a wave to the rim and back along a painted path. Stand behind a fallen column, or off the band entirely. Columns are the only cover in this room, so choose yours before the slam.",
      threadweaver: "The slam sent a wave to the rim and back along a painted band, and I pulled my stitches behind a fallen column, tight, off the path. A neat seam, and the water went round us.",
      marionettist: "After the fist, the sea made an exit to the rim, and then an entrance back, along a path painted on the stage. The company took cover behind the fallen columns, in the wings. (A very wet reprise.)",
      cleric: "After the fist fell, a wave ran out to the rim and came back, and the whole path was painted. I gathered everyone behind the fallen columns, out of its road, and mended them from there.",
      grovekeeper: "The slam sent a wave out to the rim and back, like a tide in a narrow bay, the whole path painted. A fallen column breaks it for whoever stands behind. My lot stood behind the columns, off the band.",
      chronomancer: "The wave goes out on the slam, and comes back from the rim a little later. The path was painted, both ways. We took cover behind a fallen column, off the band, until the echo passed.",
      tidecaller: "The slam sent the water to the rim and the rim sent it back, a rip along a painted road. A fallen column breaks it for whoever stands behind. We stood behind the columns.",
      lanternkeeper: "After the slam a wave went out to the rim and came back, along a painted road. I carried our lights behind a fallen column, which breaks it, and the others followed. It was already burning when they got there.",
      kenseier: "After the fist, a wave to the rim and back, and a blade cannot turn water. The path is painted, wide. A fallen column breaks it. We stood behind the columns, off the band, and outlasted it.",
      houndmaster: "Slam, then a wave out to the rim and back. Path painted wide. A fallen column breaks it for whoever's behind. Whistled the dogs round behind one. Stayed there, all of us. Snug as a barn in a gale.",
    } },
    'Undertow Grip': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A shadow fell on one of us, and a hand closed round them and would not let go. I turned on the hand with the rest of the line and broke it before it could slam them. The healer kept them standing meanwhile.",
      gloomsworn: "A great hand closed on one of us and would not let go. That grip is no stranger to me. We struck it down together before he slammed his prize into the stone. The healer kept them up while we worked. Break it before.",
      thresher: "A shadow falls on one of us, dear, and then a great hand closes round them and holds. Everybody turn and break the hand before he slams them into the stone. The healer keeps the poor soul up.",
      bloodreaver: "The hand closed on one of us and they bled for it, which I admire in principle! But the slam after is a kill. We all broke the hand before then. A good fight over a friend.",
      runeguard: "A shadow falls on one of us, and the hand follows; the shadow cannot be outrun. Once the hand closes, we break it together before the slam, while the healer sustains the held one.",
      gorgemaw: "A hand reached up from the sea and took one guest from the table, and held them for the main course. We all fell on the hand together and broke it before the slam. The healer kept the guest warm. Chewy.",
      oathbroker: "A hand is laid upon one of my co-signatories, whose shadow gives notice of it. It holds the party until it is broken, and a slam is owed if it is not. All parties strike the hand together. The healer sustains the held party.",
      ironpalm: "A shadow fell. The hand closed on one of us. It held, and we answered by breaking it, all together, before the slam. The healer kept them breathing.",
      ranger: "Shadow on one of us. Can't outrun it. Hand closes and holds. Everyone on the hand, broke it before the slam. Healer kept the one held on their feet.",
      shadowblade: "A shadow fell on one of us, and I was glad it wasn't mine. The hand closed. We all turned on it, quickly, before the slam. The healer kept them standing. I was glad again, and a little ashamed. Next time, who knows.",
      pyromancer: "A great shadow fell on one of us and a hand rose from the sea and CLOSED on them! We all lit it up at once and broke it before the slam. The healer kept them on their feet. I was a little shaken afterwards, and pretended not to be.",
      thermist: "The shadow falls on one of us, the hand closes, and nobody outruns it. Everyone on the hand; break it before the slam. It gave, and I was breathless, hot to the fingers.",
      driftblade: "A shadow fell on one of us and followed, and no one outruns a shadow, and then the hand closed and held, so we all turned and tore into it with everything we had and broke it before the slam, and the healer kept them up all the while.",
      alembist: "A hand closed on one of us and bled them, from a shadow that cannot be outrun. Everyone onto the hand at once, break it before the slam, while I keep the held one topped up. The shadow is a warning, not a place to run from.",
      threadweaver: "A shadow fell on one of my stitches, and then a great hand closed on them. I kept the thread tight and the bleeding mended while the rest of us cut the hand through before the slam. A hand like that has no right to my seam.",
      marionettist: "A shadow fell on one of the company, and a great hand rose from the sea and took them offstage. The company turned on the hand at once and broke it before the slam. The healer kept the held one standing. (A rescue, not a bow.)",
      cleric: "A shadow fell on one of my dear ones, and a great hand closed on them. I kept the light on them, steady, while we all fell on the hand and broke it before the slam. Not one of us left them.",
      grovekeeper: "A shadow fell on one of my lot like a cloud before hail, and a hand closed on them. I kept the mending growing while the rest of us broke the hand before the slam. It is a long hold, and the mending has to be rooted early.",
      chronomancer: "The shadow falls, and a beat later the hand closes, and a few beats after that it slams. We broke it before the last. I kept the held one up while we did. Quick work, and no one needed undoing.",
      tidecaller: "A shadow fell on one of us like a squall on the water, and the undertow took them by the hand. We all turned on it together and broke it before the slam. I kept the water high around them meanwhile.",
      lanternkeeper: "A shadow fell on one of us, and a great hand took them. I kept a light on them the whole while, and the rest of us broke the hand before the slam. One held, three working.",
      kenseier: "A shadow falls, then the hand closes, and a blade can cut a hand but not a shadow. We struck it down together, stroke on stroke, before the slam. The healer held the held one up.",
      houndmaster: "Shadow fell on one of us, then a hand closed on them. All on the hand at once, the dogs too, and broke it before the slam. Healer kept them standing. Like pulling a calf from a bog.",
    } },
    'Sunwheel Unbound': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He grew the wheel to the size of a house and threw it; the road was wide and bounced off the walls and the broken stones. Two blue rings, one on the way and one at the end. A friend took one and I the other. The line stood well off the road.",
      gloomsworn: "The wheel grew huge and the road with it, bouncing off the walls and the broken stones, with two blue rings on its path, one on the way and one at the end. Two of us stood in them. I took one. The rest kept far off the road.",
      thresher: "He throws a wheel as big as a house, dear, and the road is wide, with two blue rings: one on the way, one at the end. Two of us wait in them; the rest keep well off the road, which the broken stones turn like the walls.",
      bloodreaver: "The wheel grew to the size of a barn! Two blue rings on its road, one on the way and one at the end. I stood in one, a friend in the other, and we each took a hit. The rest stayed off the wide road, which the stones turn too.",
      runeguard: "The wheel grown huge, its road wide, its bounces many, the broken stones turning it as the walls do. Two blue rings are inscribed on the path, one in the middle and one at its end; two of us catch, and the rest stand far from the road.",
      gorgemaw: "A plate the size of a table, skimmed off the walls and the broken stones, with two blue rings on its route: one on the way and one at the end. Two guests take it, and the rest keep far from the wide route. Two courses, each underseasoned.",
      oathbroker: "The instrument is enlarged, its route widened and turned by the broken stones as by the walls, and two blue rings entered on it: one along the way and one at the end. Two parties stand in them and take delivery in full. The remainder keep far from the widened route.",
      ironpalm: "He threw a giant wheel and spoke it across the walls and the stones. Two blue rings on the road: one on the way, one at the end. Two of us stood in them. The rest stayed far from the road. We answered it twice.",
      ranger: "Huge wheel. Wide road, many bounces, walls and stones both. Two blue rings: one on the way, one at the end. Two of us in the rings, the rest well off the road. Wide, but easy to read.",
      shadowblade: "The mark grew his wheel to a monster, and two blue rings were drawn on the road: one on the way and one at the end. Two of us took them. I was not one, and kept well off the road, which the stones turn as well as the walls.",
      pyromancer: "The wheel grew enormous and the road was a stage-wide stripe, glowing like a warning, with two blue rings: one on the way and one at the end! Two of us stood in them and caught it. The rest kept well off the road. The stones bounce it as well as the walls. I applauded.",
      thermist: "A huge wheel, a wide road, two blue rings on it: one on the way, one at the end. Two of us in the rings, the rest far off the road. The stones turn it too, and it was wider than my nerve.",
      driftblade: "The wheel came wide as a barn and bounced off the rim and every broken stone, and I went round its road with room to spare, because it was drawn first, while two of us stood in the blue rings, one on the way and one at the end.",
      alembist: "Two doses, not one: a wheel the size of a wagon, many bounces off walls and stones, two blue rings, one on the way and one at the end. Both catchers get mended beforehand and everyone else stays well off the wide road.",
      threadweaver: "A wheel as big as a wagon, and a road as wide as a bolt of cloth, turned by the stones like the walls. Two blue rings on it, one on the way and one at the end. Two of my stitches caught it; the rest kept off the cloth.",
      marionettist: "The prop grew to the size of the set, and the blocking was chalked wide across the stage, with two blue marks: one on the way and one at the end. Two of the company took them. The rest stayed in the wings; the fallen stones turn it like the walls.",
      cleric: "The wheel grew huge and its road wide, turned by the broken stones as by the walls, with two blue rings on it, one on the way and one at the end. Two of my dear ones stood in them, and I laid the light on both. The rest kept far off the road.",
      grovekeeper: "The wheel grew big as a haystack and rolled off the rim and every broken stone like a landslide, the road wide and drawn first, with two blue rings on it, one on the way and one at the end. Two of my lot caught it. The rest kept off. Mending rooted in both.",
      chronomancer: "The huge wheel has two blue rings on its road, one on the way, one at the end, and two of us took them, a beat apart. I mended both early. The rest stayed off the wide road, the stones turning it as the walls do. I did say that already, did I not.",
      tidecaller: "A wheel as big as a breaker, skipping off the rim and the broken stones, the road wide and drawn first, with two blue rings on it, one on the way and one at the end. Two of us caught it. I kept the water high on both.",
      lanternkeeper: "The wheel grew huge, and two blue rings were drawn on its road, one on the way and one at the end, the broken stones turning it as the walls do. I hung a light on each of the two who stood in them. The rest kept off the road. Two catchers, two lights.",
      kenseier: "A giant wheel, and a wide road, turned by the stones as by the walls, with two beats to it: a blue ring on the way and one at the end. Two of us met it as it landed, one at each. The rest stayed far off the road. A big count, honestly kept.",
      houndmaster: "Big lad grew the wheel to a cart, road wide, bounces plenty off walls and stones, two blue rings on it: one on the way, one at the end. Two of us took them. Rest of us, dogs too, stayed well off the road. Like keeping dogs off a haywain.",
    } },
    'Deep Call': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The sea heaved and reached every one of us, and dragged us in toward the middle. No shield turns it. We came to it mended, and as it let go I led the fist away from the others, because what he sends next finds whoever is bunched.",
      gloomsworn: "The sea called, and the whole ring heard it, and it dragged us toward the middle like mourners to a grave. We came mended, and spread out the moment it let go. What he sends next finds a crowd.",
      thresher: "The sea heaves and calls, dear, and drags every one of us in toward the middle. Come to it mended, and then spread out at once, because what he throws next goes for the crowd. Do mind the pull.",
      bloodreaver: "The sea called and hit all of us, and dragged us into a heap in the middle! Nothing to dodge. I came mended, and when it let go I bolted out of the heap, because he throws at the heap next.",
      runeguard: "The sea heaves, and the call reaches every one of us and drags us toward the middle. Be mended beforehand, and spread the moment it lets go, for the next blow is aimed at the gathering.",
      gorgemaw: "The sea heaved like a great stomach and drew every guest toward the middle of the table. No one can swallow it for another. We came mended, and scattered the instant it let go, for the next course lands on the crowd. An acquired taste.",
      oathbroker: "The call is a general summons upon every party, payable at once, with delivery to the middle. Arrive whole. Disperse on release: the next claim is made wherever the parties are gathered.",
      ironpalm: "The sea spoke to all of us and drew us toward the middle. There was nothing to turn. We were mended, and we took it. When it let go we moved apart, because the next word falls on the crowd.",
      ranger: "Sea heaves. Whole ring takes it, drags everyone toward the middle. Mended first. Spread the moment it lets go; the next shot lands on the group. No cover.",
      shadowblade: "The sea called and found every one of us, and dragged us toward the middle like a crowd at a stage door. I came mended, and slipped out of the knot as it let go, because what follows finds the knot.",
      pyromancer: "The sea heaved and called and hit all of us, and dragged us into a pile in the middle! I came mended, and the moment it let go I ran out of the pile, because his next throw goes for piles. Thoroughly sprayed, and thoroughly offended.",
      thermist: "Everyone takes the sea's call and the pull gathers us in the middle. Mended first. We were all in a clump, and a clump runs hot. Spread the moment it lets go; the next blow wants the crowd.",
      driftblade: "The sea heaved and caught everyone, no running round it, and dragged us toward the middle, so I went in mended, through it, and out wide the moment it let go, because the next blow wants the crowd and I do not stand in one.",
      alembist: "A call across the whole ring, then a drag toward the middle. I mixed the mending before, not after, and we dispersed the moment it let go, because the next blow is aimed at the gathering. Never queue at the counter.",
      threadweaver: "The sea called along every thread at once and dragged us all in toward the middle. I mended my stitches before, not after, and let the threads go slack the moment it released us, so we spread. The next blow wants the knot.",
      marionettist: "The sea heaved, the house shook, and the whole company was dragged to centre stage. We came mended, and scattered to the wings as it let go, because the next cue lands on the crowd. (Do not linger in the spotlight.)",
      cleric: "The sea heaved and called, and it came over every one of us and drew us toward the middle. I mended before it came, not after, and called them apart the moment it let go. The next blow wants a crowd.",
      grovekeeper: "The sea heaved like a field in a gale and drew us in toward the middle. I'd planted on everyone before it, and we spread out the moment it let go, because the next blow wants a bunch of us.",
      chronomancer: "The call comes as he opens his arms, and the pull on its heels. I had everyone mended just before, and we spread on the next beat, because the blow after it wants the gathering.",
      tidecaller: "The sea heaved all at once and drew us in toward the middle, the way a harbour fills. I brought the water up before it came, and we spread out as it ebbed, because what he throws next finds a crowd.",
      lanternkeeper: "The sea called over every one of us and dragged us in toward the middle. I hung a light on each before it came, and as it let go we spread out, each carrying our own. The next blow wants a crowd.",
      kenseier: "A heave from the sea that no blade turns, and the pull after it. We stood mended and outlasted it. Then we parted on the next beat, because the stroke that follows seeks the gathering.",
      houndmaster: "Sea heaved and dragged the lot of us, dogs too, in toward the middle. Mended beforehand. Soon as it let go I sent the dogs and everyone out wide, because the next throw wants the pack bunched. Sit. Then spread.",
    } },
    'The Final Bell': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The bell tolled, and the whole room went with it. He stopped holding back, and no shield turns that. We had been too slow. Every opening he gave us, we should have hit harder.",
      gloomsworn: "The last bell rang for all of us. The bout has a limit, as every watch has, and we ran past it. Every watch ends, and this one ended with us still at it. We were not through in time.",
      thresher: "At the end the bell tolls, dear, and he stops waiting, and nothing is tidy after that. Be done before it, and use every pose he strikes. His name is on the list.",
      bloodreaver: "The final bell rang and he hit every one of us at once, and nobody got up from that one! We were slow. Every opening he gave us was a chance to hit him harder, and we wasted a few. Be done first, my friend.",
      runeguard: "The bell sounds at a fixed hour, and the end is the end. Finish before it, and use every opening he gives us in full; the hour does not move.",
      gorgemaw: "The last bell rang, the kitchen closed, and the last course arrived at every plate at once. We had dawdled over the starters. Eat faster, and bite deepest in the openings. The clock is a rude host.",
      oathbroker: "The term expires: the final bell, at an hour fixed in advance. Our performance fell short and the forfeit fell on all. The openings he allowed were left unused. Use every one next time.",
      ironpalm: "The bell rang, and he ran out of patience, and it fell on all of us. We had answered too slowly. Every opening he gave was a word we could have said louder. Be finished before the last one.",
      ranger: "Bell. Whole arena goes under. Too slow. Wasted openings when he posed. Hit hard, hit then, be done before the bell. No line, no time.",
      shadowblade: "The final bell rang and the whole arena fell in on us. Not even I could hide. We had spent his poses on manners. Strike hard when he is open, and be gone before the bell. A strict timekeeper, that bell.",
      pyromancer: "The final bell RANG and so did my ears and we all went down together! Every pose he struck was a stage for a bigger spell, and I wasted some on modesty. Be quick, burn hard, and be done before it.",
      thermist: "Final bell. The whole arena goes cold and dark at once, and that is that. Too slow. Every opening wasted pushed the end later. Hit hard when he is open, and finish early.",
      driftblade: "The bell rang and the room came down on everyone and there was nowhere to run, and I ran anyway, and it caught me, because we were slow and the bell does not wait, and every opening he gave us could have been fewer laps.",
      alembist: "The final bell, at a fixed hour. We were slow, and his openings were not spent in full. Next batch: hit hard whenever he poses, and be done early. Shelf note: this brew spoils.",
      threadweaver: "The final bell rang and every thread was cut at once. We had left too many openings half used. A tidy seam and an early finish, next time: hit him hard every time he poses.",
      marionettist: "The final bell, the house lights out, and the curtain on the wrong side, with the company still on stage. We had wasted the pauses in his act. Next time, strike in every opening, and be done before the bell. (The critics will not be kind.)",
      cleric: "The final bell rang and not one of us got up. We had been too slow, and the openings he gave us were not used in full. I should have urged them harder. Forgive me, all of you. Next time, early.",
      grovekeeper: "The final bell rang like a late frost and everything died at once. The season ran on because we wasted his openings. Next time we strike hard whenever he poses, and finish early.",
      chronomancer: "The final bell rings at the same hour, however many times we undo it. We were slow, and the openings went half used. Next time, which was last time, we hit hard when he poses, and finish early.",
      tidecaller: "The final bell rang like the tide going out for good, and everything with it. We had been slow, and wasted his openings. A short fight and a hard-hitting one, next time.",
      lanternkeeper: "The final bell rang and the lamps all went out at once. We ran out of oil: too slow, too many openings half spent. Next time, hit hard whenever he stops to pose, and finish while the lamps are still warm.",
      kenseier: "The final bell is a stroke without a count, and it comes at a fixed hour. We were late. Every opening he gave was a beat we could have struck on. A master keeps time; next time, so do I.",
      houndmaster: "Bell rang and the whole lot of us went out with it. Too slow by half. Wasted his poses. Should've hit hard each time he stopped to show off and been finished first.",
    } },
    'Twin Wheels': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "On the hard nights he throws two, one after the other, and the roads cross. Two blue rings, well apart; the second road wears two dots. Two of us took the rings. The rest let the first pass and crossed before the second arrived.",
      gloomsworn: "On the hard nights he throws two wheels, a breath apart, and the roads cross. Two blue rings, far apart; I took one. The rest watched the first go by, then crossed the painted junction in the quiet before the second.",
      thresher: "On the hard night, dear, two wheels, a heartbeat apart, and their roads cross. The one with two little dots on its road leaves second. Two of us in the blue rings, and everyone else crosses the junction only after the first has gone through. Mind the second!",
      bloodreaver: "On the hard nights, two wheels, one right after the other, roads crossing! The second one's road wears two dots. Two of us took the blue rings. The rest hopped the crossing once the first had roared past, and before the second came. A doubly good one.",
      runeguard: "On the harder nights two wheels are thrown in sequence, their roads crossing; the second road is marked with two dots at its foot. Two blue rings, two catchers. The rest pass the crossing in the gap between the wheels, and not a step after.",
      gorgemaw: "On the hard nights, two plates, one after the other, skimming across each other's routes. The second route is marked with two dots, like a second helping. Two guests in the blue rings; the rest cross the junction between courses.",
      oathbroker: "On the harder terms, two instruments are thrown in sequence, their routes crossing; the second route is marked with two dots at its foot. Two parties receive the blue rings. The remaining parties may cross between the two wheels, and are advised not to linger.",
      ironpalm: "On hard nights, two wheels, one after the other, their roads crossing. The second wears two dots. Two of us stood in the blue rings. The rest crossed in the quiet between the wheels. Breathe, then step.",
      ranger: "Hard nights: two wheels, one after the other, roads crossing. Second road marked with two dots. Two catchers in the blue rings. The rest cross the junction after the first has passed and before the second. Read both.",
      shadowblade: "On the hard nights the mark throws two, one a breath behind the other, roads crossing. Two blue rings; two of us took them. I crossed the junction in the gap between the wheels, after the first and before the second.",
      pyromancer: "On the hard nights he throws TWO wheels, one right behind the other, crossing each other! Two blue rings, far apart, two of us to catch. The rest found the crossing in the gap between them and ran it.",
      thermist: "Hard nights: two wheels, one after the other. Two blue rings, two catchers, and a clear moment at the crossing between the wheels. I ran it a heartbeat early and felt the first wheel pass at my shoulder.",
      driftblade: "On the hard nights two wheels came one after the other, and the second road wore two dots. Two of us took the blue rings, and I crossed in the quiet between the wheels, which is the best place there is, and nothing touched me.",
      alembist: "Two wheels in sequence, roads crossing, the second road marked with two dots. Two catchers stand in the blue rings, both mended beforehand; everyone else crosses the junction once the first wheel has passed, and never after the second.",
      threadweaver: "On the hard nights two wheels came one after the other, their roads crossing like two seams; the second seam wore two stitches at its foot. Two of my stitches in the blue rings. The rest passed the crossing between the wheels.",
      marionettist: "On the hard nights, a double entrance, one after the other: two wheels, roads crossing at centre stage, the second chalked with two dots. Two of the company on the blue marks; the rest crossed between the entrances. (A very busy scene.)",
      cleric: "On the harder nights he threw two wheels, one after the other, and their roads crossed. Two blue rings, and two of my dear ones in them; I laid the light on both. The rest crossed in the quiet between the wheels, never after.",
      grovekeeper: "On the hard nights, two wheels, one after the other, like two storms crossing. The second road wore two dots. Two of my lot caught them in the blue rings. The rest crossed the junction in the lull between. Both catchers had the mending rooted in them beforehand.",
      chronomancer: "On the hard nights two wheels come in sequence, their roads crossing; the second road is dotted twice. Two blue rings, and two of us catching, a beat apart. The rest crossed in the gap between. Both were mended early.",
      tidecaller: "On the hard nights two wheels skip across the bay one after the other, their roads crossing. Two blue rings, far apart. The rest of us crossed in the slack water between them, after the first wave of it and before the second.",
      lanternkeeper: "On the hard nights two wheels came one behind the other, and their roads crossed; the second wore two small dots. I hung a light on each of the two in the blue rings. The rest crossed in the dark between the wheels. Two lights, two catchers.",
      kenseier: "On the hard nights, two wheels in sequence, with two counts that cross; the second is marked with two dots. Two of us met them with the blade as they landed. The rest crossed in the pause between the wheels. A courteous double.",
      houndmaster: "Hard nights, two wheels, one after the other, roads crossing. Second road wears two dots. Two of us took the blue rings. Rest of us, dogs too, crossed the gate in the gap between wheels, not before the first, not after the second.",
    } },
    'Double Grip': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "On the hard nights both hands come, and a shadow falls on two of us. Two hands, two of us gripped. The line split in two and broke them both before the slams. The healer kept both held standing.",
      gloomsworn: "On the hard nights both hands reach for two of us. The watch split in two and broke the hands together, before either slam. The healer worked between them. Two grips, and neither of them mine.",
      thresher: "On the hard night, dear, both his hands come, and a shadow falls on two of us. We split in two at once and broke both hands before the slams. The healer keeps both poor souls up.",
      bloodreaver: "On the hard nights both hands came, two of us gripped and bleeding! I split off with half the party and broke mine before the slam. The other half broke theirs. A double fight over friends.",
      runeguard: "On the harder nights both hands come, a shadow on two of us. We divide the party, half to each hand, and break both before either slam; the healer sustains both held.",
      gorgemaw: "On the hard nights both hands reached for the table, and two guests were taken. We split in half and fell on both hands at once, and broke them before the slams. The healer fed both guests. A double portion, and tough.",
      oathbroker: "On the harder terms both hands are laid, on two named parties. The company divides into two and break both hands before either slam falls. The healer sustains both held parties.",
      ironpalm: "On hard nights both hands closed, on two of us. We divided and answered both together, and broke them before the slams. The healer kept both on their feet. I breathed for two.",
      ranger: "Hard nights: both hands. Two of us gripped. Split the party, one hand each, break both before the slams. Healer works between them. Same job, twice over.",
      shadowblade: "On the hard nights both hands come, and two shadows fell, neither on me. I joined the nearer hand, and we broke it, and the others broke the second, before the slams. Greedy of him, asking for two at once.",
      pyromancer: "On the hard nights BOTH hands reached up and took two of us! We split in two and lit them both up at once, and broke the hands before the slams. The healer kept both alive. Rather thrilled.",
      thermist: "Hard nights: both hands, two shadows, two held. Split the party, half to each, and break both before the slams. I joined the nearest hand, colder for it, and steady.",
      driftblade: "On the hard nights both hands closed on two of us and the party split in two and fell on both hands at once, and broke them before the slams, and the healer ran between the held ones, which I respect.",
      alembist: "Two hands, two held, two slams pending. Split the party, one hand each, and break both before the slams. The healer cannot be in two places, so I threw doses across the gap and picked a side for the rest.",
      threadweaver: "On the hard nights both hands came and took two of my stitches. We split the hem in two and cut both hands through before the slams, and I ran thread to both held ones. A long stretch of thread, and nobody frayed.",
      marionettist: "On the hard nights, a double seizure: both hands, two of the company taken offstage. The company split in two and rescued both before the slams. The healer worked the wings between them. (An ambitious double rescue.)",
      cleric: "On the harder nights both hands closed on two of my dear ones. We divided at once, half to each, and broke both hands before the slams. I kept the light on both, one then the other.",
      grovekeeper: "On the hard nights both hands came, like two storms on one field. We split in half and broke them both before the slams. I kept the mending growing on both held. There is no second chance with a hand that size.",
      chronomancer: "On the hard nights both hands come, a beat apart, and two of us are held. The party splits, and breaks both before the slams. I healed one on the first beat and the other on the next. A busy pair of beats.",
      tidecaller: "On the hard nights both hands rose from the sea at once, and two of us were taken. The party split, half to each, and broke them before the slams. I sent the water to both.",
      lanternkeeper: "On the hard nights both hands came, and two of us were held. I kept a light on each of them while the party split and broke both hands before the slams. Two held, two lights.",
      kenseier: "On the hard nights both hands closed, on two of us. A blade can only cut one at a time, so we split, half to each, and broke both before the slams. The healer kept both standing.",
      houndmaster: "Hard nights, both hands, two of us held. Split the party, dogs and all, one hand each. Broke both before the slams. Healer ran between them. Like working two gates at once.",
    } },
    'Riposte': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "On the hard nights, I caught the wheel and he kicked it straight back from where I stood, along a new road. I read it and stepped off the spot at once, and the line stayed off the new road.",
      gloomsworn: "On the hard nights the wheel I caught was kicked back from the same spot, along a fresh road, bouncing twice. I walked out of the blue ring before it moved. The rest kept off the new road.",
      thresher: "On the hard night, dear, a caught wheel is kicked straight back from where it was caught, along a brand-new road. So the catcher steps out of the ring and everyone reads the new line.",
      bloodreaver: "On the hard nights I caught the wheel and he kicked it right back from my feet along a new road! I loved it. I stepped off the spot at once, and the others stayed off the new road. An encore for the same wheel.",
      runeguard: "On the harder nights a caught wheel is kicked back from the very spot where it was caught, along a new painted road. The catcher leaves the ring at once, and everyone reads the new road.",
      gorgemaw: "On the hard nights the plate I caught was sent back from the table, along a new route, painted. I rose from my seat at once, and the others kept off the new route. A second helping of the same dish, and a nasty one.",
      oathbroker: "On the harder terms a caught wheel is returned from the point of delivery, along a fresh route entered in advance. The catcher vacates the ring at once; all parties stay clear of the new route.",
      ironpalm: "On hard nights, a caught wheel is kicked back along a new road, from where it was caught. It asked again. I left the spot at once and the others kept off the new road.",
      ranger: "Hard nights: caught wheel gets kicked back from the same spot, new road, painted, bounces. Catcher steps out at once. Everyone off the new road. Second try, same rule: read it.",
      shadowblade: "On the hard nights, after the catch, the wheel is kicked back from the same spot, along a new road. The catcher slipped out of the ring at once. The rest of us read the new road. The mark always asks for an encore.",
      pyromancer: "On the hard nights the wheel I caught was kicked right back from my feet along a new road, and it glowed like a forge at once! I stepped out of the ring, the others kept off the new road. My hands were steady; the rest of me was loudly not.",
      thermist: "Hard nights: the catch is not the end. The wheel is kicked back from the same spot along a new road. Step out of the ring, and everyone read the new road. I was a heartbeat slow and felt the scald.",
      driftblade: "On the hard nights the wheel I caught got kicked back along a new road from the very spot I stood, so I ran out of the ring the moment I caught it, through the gap, and the others had already read the new road.",
      alembist: "A caught wheel, kicked back from the point of catch along a new painted road. The catcher leaves the ring at once and everyone stays off the new road. Mend the catcher after the leaving, not before. A tidy little trap; I admire it.",
      threadweaver: "On the hard nights the wheel was kicked back from where it was caught, along a new seam. The catcher stepped out at once and the rest of my stitches stayed off the new line. And mind the catcher.",
      marionettist: "On the hard nights, an encore: the caught wheel is kicked back from the same mark along a new road, chalked afresh. The catcher exits at once and the company reads the new chalk. (The Doll had already left.)",
      cleric: "On the harder nights, the wheel is kicked back from where it was caught, along a new road. I called the catcher out of the ring at once, and the others kept off the new line.",
      grovekeeper: "On the hard nights the wheel was kicked back from the spot it was caught, along a new road, like a second gust after the first. The catcher stepped out at once and my lot kept off the new road.",
      chronomancer: "On the hard nights, the wheel comes back hard on the catch, from the same spot, along a new road. The catcher stepped out on that beat, and the rest read the new road. I had told them already.",
      tidecaller: "On the hard nights the caught wheel was kicked back from the same spot, like a wave sent back from a rock, along a new painted road. The catcher stepped out of the ring and the rest kept off.",
      lanternkeeper: "On the hard nights the wheel was kicked back from where it was caught, along a new road. I picked the catcher's light up and set it down off the new road, and they followed. Nobody had to find it in the dark.",
      kenseier: "On the hard nights the caught wheel is kicked back, from the very spot, along a fresh road. A second count after the first. The catcher stepped out of the ring, and the rest kept off the new road. A fine reprise.",
      houndmaster: "Hard nights, the wheel's kicked back from where it was caught, along a new road. Catcher stepped out of the ring at once. Rest of us, dogs too, kept off the new road. Like a dog sent back out.",
    } },
  },
};
